231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Natural and life sciences, social sciences, and teacher training all approach sustainability differently. Measures that are easy to quantify in the sciences may be harder to evaluate in the humanities. Your proposal needs to speak across these differences.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Fragmented student engagement)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Many sustainability initiatives exist, but there is limited coordination, visibility, and shared knowledge between them. Groups like FlyingLess and BNE@UP have been recently revived. Your concept could build on or connect to existing efforts rather than starting from scratch.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Institutional and budgetary constraints)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The university has different decision-making processes across faculties, and some campuses \(especially Neues Palais\) are subject to heritage protection rules. Resources for physical interventions are limited. Low-cost, step-by-step approaches that can start small and grow are more likely to succeed.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Communication and acceptance)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Different levels of knowledge and attitudes towards sustainability across campus require targeted communication. What works for biology students may not resonate in law or economics. Think about how to make your concept visible and relatable across disciplines.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
